# Build context = monorepo root (the Caddy image with the admin, the builder image and the Node development base).
# Whitelist: only what the Dockerfiles copy gets in. That keeps the context at KBs instead of hundreds of MB, no secret
# or local data (.env, SQLite, media) can slip into an image, and touching something unrelated (docs/, the API, which
# has its own context) does not invalidate the cache.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!tooling
!packages
!apps/admin
!apps/web
!apps/builder
!infra/caddy/Caddyfile

# Within what is allowed, nothing generated on your machine (Windows node_modules, builds) and no tests: the images
# install and build their own.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.astro
**/test
**/*.tsbuildinfo
